#!/bin/bash
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Open a shell with the lab commands that are installed on this image.
# Names only. This is not a guide for using the tools.
cat <<'EOF'
Laden OS lab tools are on this image for authorized work.

Kali commands people actually use:
  nmap, zenmap     network scanner and its GUI
  masscan, naabu   fast port scanners
  amass, subfinder, httpx, theharvester, dnsrecon
  responder is not installed. Its package pulls a 1.2 GiB MinGW compiler.
  enum4linux-ng, smbmap, smbclient, impacket-*
  netexec, nxc     Active Directory testing
  bloodhound-python, bloodhound-ce-python
                   collectors only. The BloodHound GUI is not installed.
  certipy, kerbrute
  burpsuite, zaproxy, sqlmap
  gobuster, ffuf, feroxbuster, nikto, wpscan, nuclei, whatweb
  john, hashcat, hydra, hashid, crunch
  aircrack-ng, hcxdumptool, wifite, reaver, bully, pixiewps, kismet, bettercap
  msfconsole, searchsploit, mitmproxy

Forensic and reverse-engineering commands:
  wireshark, tcpdump
  autopsy, guymager
  mmls, fls        from sleuthkit
  testdisk, photorec
  binwalk, foremost, scalpel, exiftool, bulk_extractor
  vol              volatility3
  yara, ssdeep, hashdeep
  dc3dd, dcfldd, ewfacquire
  python-plaso     timeline tools
  regripper, chkrootkit, rkhunter, unhide, chntpw, stegseek
  r2, iaito, ghidra

seclists is not installed. John ships a small wordlist.
The terminal is lcp. Alt+T opens it. Alt+Q shows or hides it.
Chromium is the default browser and opens https://laden.no.
The full BlackArch catalogue is not installed.
More tools from the enabled BlackArch repository can be added with pacman.
EOF
exec fish -l
